{"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Add Feature Flags"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"How-to Guides","anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"text":" is a domain plugin that owns a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState"},{"text":" slice, fetches a Swidux-defined JSON wire format via a provider-agnostic ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and answers reads against state. Bucketing is pure FNV-1a — same input always produces the same bucket, no network round-trip per read. Local overrides give QA a one-action toggle that wins over remote evaluation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For an API-level reference, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". For where domain plugins fit in the dispatch cycle, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Before you start","type":"heading","anchor":"Before-you-start","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide assumes you have a Swidux app already wired up — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore"},{"type":"text","text":" exist and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If you’re not there yet, follow "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"},{"text":" first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You also need somewhere to host a JSON file. Any URL works — Cloudflare Pages, R2, S3, a Worker, your own backend. The plugin doesn’t care. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Examples\/ConfigWorker\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a runnable Cloudflare Worker that serves feature-flag ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"text":" killswitch config for every app in a portfolio from one URL and one KV namespace, keyed ","type":"text"},{"code":"GET \/<appID>\/<resource>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — point this plugin at ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product to your app target in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxFeatureFlags\",","    ]",")"]},{"text":"Step 2: Add a state slice and action case","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-2-Add-a-state-slice-and-action-case","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxFeatureFlags","","@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @Slice var featureFlags: FeatureFlagsState = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case featureFlags(FeatureFlagsAction)","    \/\/ ... your other cases","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"name":"Tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" is needed in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file that touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.featureFlags.*"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — including views that read flags for display. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" re-exports core Swidux only, not plugin modules. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"tip"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 3: Hydrate state and register the plugin","anchor":"Step-3-Hydrate-state-and-register-the-plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"At app launch, hydrate state from your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"text":" (so the install ID and last-known-good config survive cold launches), then register the plugin:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let kv = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore()","let initial = AppState(","    featureFlags: .hydrated(from: kv)",")","","let store = Store(initialState: initial, reducer: AppReducer())","","\/\/ With the Examples\/ConfigWorker setup this is the shared portfolio URL:","\/\/ \"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags\". Any URL returning FeatureFlagsConfig works.","let configURL = URL(static: \"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags\")","","let flags = FeatureFlagsPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.featureFlags,","    action: AppAction.featureFlags,","    extractAction: { if case .featureFlags(let a) = $0 { return a } else { return nil } },","    service: HTTPFeatureFlagsService(url: configURL),","    keyValueStore: kv",")","store.register(plugin: flags)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 4: Declare typed flag keys","anchor":"Step-4-Declare-typed-flag-keys"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare each flag once on a namespace so reads are type-safe:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["extension BoolFlag {","    static let newOnboarding = BoolFlag(\"new_onboarding\")","}","","enum CheckoutVariant: String { case control, treatment }","","extension VariantFlag where Variant == CheckoutVariant {","    static let checkoutLayout = VariantFlag(\"checkout_layout\", default: .control)","}","","extension ValueFlag where Value == Int {","    static let maxFreeUploads = ValueFlag(\"max_free_uploads\", default: 5)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Step-5-Read-flags-from-views","text":"Step 5: Read flags from views","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["if store.featureFlags.isEnabled(.newOnboarding) {","    NewOnboardingView()","}","","let layout = store.featureFlags.variant(of: .checkoutLayout)","let cap = store.featureFlags.value(of: .maxFreeUploads)"]},{"anchor":"Step-6-Refresh-on-foreground","text":"Step 6: Refresh on foreground","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin debounces ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refresh"},{"text":" against the configured ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RefreshPolicy"},{"text":", so it’s safe to dispatch on every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scenePhase"},{"text":" transition:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .active { store.send(.featureFlags(.refresh)) }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For wire format, bucketing, and exposure tracking details, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store."}],"title":"Add a Version Killswitch","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","abstract":[{"text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":" macro — no hand-written ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" classes, database actors, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"title":"Add Persistence","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}],"title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify.","type":"text"}],"title":"Add Analytics","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","title":"Add a Paywall"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"text":" with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"},{"text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","title":"Add iCloud Sync"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"title":"Swidux","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"title":"Getting Started with Swidux","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Install the bundled ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-ref"},{"text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and